  {
   "id": "typical",
   "title": "Typical application",
   "page": 9,
   "description": "A microcontroller or other logic running from 3.3 V or 5 V drives both gate inputs; the gate runs from a regulated 5 V rail with a 0.1 µF bypass capacitor, and its output drives a 5 V accessory powered from that same rail. The TTL input thresholds let a 3.3 V source be lifted to a 5 V signal.",
   "parts": [
    {
     "ref": "U1",
     "type": "ic",
